scene torus.esn

# At time 0 the torus sits tilted toward the camera. The hole and the
# corners show the background gradient; the left of the ring lands on an
# orange check and the right on a blue one, both lit from the upper right.
# The two rasterizers agree on every interior pixel; edges are avoided.
frame 0.0
expect 20 20 = 0.114 0.122 0.173 0.02
expect 160 120 = 0.086 0.09 0.129 0.02
expect 60 120 = 0.698 0.427 0.196 0.04
expect 260 120 = 0.298 0.643 0.89 0.04
expect 160 200 = 0.345 0.212 0.094 0.04

# `level` sizes the graph: at two levels the second time's rows exist,
# and the 9217th triangle, past the first level's 9216, reads as one of
# the four a level-one face split into. Midpoint subdivision keeps the
# surface, so the picture is the same.
param level 2
frame 0.0
expect subdivided/2.quartered.result[9216].a = 288
expect 60 120 = 0.698 0.427 0.196 0.04
